Package: vbpm
Type: Package
Title: Variational Bayes Partially Confirmatory Measurement Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jinsong", "Chen", email = "jinsong.chen@live.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0157-5469")),
    person("Yi", "Jin", role = "aut",
           comment = "first author of the method papers and the estimator"))
Description: Regularized variational Bayes estimation of partially confirmatory
    factor-analytic measurement models (Chen, Guo, Zhang, and Pan, 2021
    <doi:10.1037/met0000293>; Jin and Chen, 2025
    <doi:10.1080/10705511.2024.2432612>). Provides variational Bayes factor
    analysis (vbfa) spanning the confirmatory-exploratory continuum via
    spike-and-slab priors on the loadings, with an optional dynamic
    (warm-started) regularization path, an orthogonal bifactor
    parameterization, and optional sparse residual (local dependence)
    estimation through a graphical spike-and-slab prior solved by QUIC.
    Companion tools compute SEM-like fit statistics and select the number of
    factors via a scale-free gain rule (Chen and Jin, 2026
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2607.07159>).
